  "res": {
   "attrs": {
    "redundancy": "1+1",
    "redundancy-note": "1+1 - mx2020 hardware guide, \"MX2020 Component Redundancy\": each host subsystem takes one or two Routing Engines in the front vertical slots 0 and 1; with two CB-REs fitted one is primary and the other backup, and the backup takes over if the primary or any part of it fails. The same bullet adds what the form drops: configured for nonstop active routing, the backup keeps its state in step with the primary and forwarding continues through a switchover"
   },
   "description": "CB-RE slots 0 and 1 at the ends of the fabric cage",
   "index-origin": 0,
   "role": "service",
   "term": "Slot"
  },
  "sfbs": {
   "attrs": {
    "redundancy": "n+1",
    "redundancy-note": "n+1 - mx2020 hardware guide, \"MX2000-SFB-S Switch Fabric Board Description\": 6 Tbps with a minimum of seven SFBs fitted, and an eighth recommended for N+1. The same entry gives the slot count these eight bays come from - up to eight SFB2s, seven needed for line rate - and the fabric is all-active, so the spare is a working plane rather than a standby. RECORDED AS THE GUIDE WRITES IT: seven-plus-one would be an arithmetic reading of two sentences and the guide itself says N+1"
   },
   "description": "Switch Fabric Board slots SFB 0-7",
